WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
- Hi, welcome to Hell!

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.930
More people tell you, go to hell.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:05.770
Here, we welcome you.

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:10.770
- I'm in Hell and I did it all
without any tech from 2019.

00:00:11.896 --> 00:00:13.979
(typing)

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:18.980
Why the hell did I end up in Hell?

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.360
Oh well, it's actually quite simple.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.150
As the clock nears 2020,

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.610
I've been thinking a lot
about how much the smartphone

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:28.540
has changed the world and
us, in the last decade.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.807
So, I challenged myself to
live with just 2010 tech

00:00:31.807 --> 00:00:33.603
for 24 hours.

00:00:35.996 --> 00:00:37.940
Does this not even have maps on it?

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.160
I asked my producer,
Kenny for some suggestions

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.440
on where to go.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.686
- I think you should go to Hell, Michigan.

00:00:43.686 --> 00:00:45.620
I grew up near there.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.620
- [Narrator] And so, we got to packing.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.384
I gathered a bunch of
gadgets I used in 2010.

00:00:50.384 --> 00:00:51.218
You hear that?

00:00:51.218 --> 00:00:53.210
Yeah, I'm bringing this.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:58.210
My BlackBerry Bold 9700,
a Zune HD, a Flip Mino HD,

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:02.030
a Cannon point and shoot,
and a Garmin Nuvi for GPS.

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.790
All of them surprisingly worked

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.550
after I charged up the batteries.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:10.550
Okay, I am putting this iPhone
in this drawer at my house,

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:14.770
and I'm leaving it here for
the next 24 hours or so.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:17.150
Challenge one, get to Hell.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:18.290
(jazz music)

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.360
And took off for the
airport to begin a series

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.070
of four challenges Kenny
had designed for me.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:25.600
Hell, it turns out, is a small township

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.435
about 60 miles out of Detroit.

00:01:27.435 --> 00:01:30.724
That meant, a flight, a drive
to stay at a hotel nearby,

00:01:30.724 --> 00:01:33.090
and then another drive to Hell.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:34.900
The flight part was easier than I thought.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.109
Look at all these people on their phones.

00:01:37.109 --> 00:01:38.530
(accordion music)

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.780
No ticket on my phone,

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.197
nothing to really do while
killing time in line.

00:01:42.197 --> 00:01:44.070
This is Brick Breaker.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.080
It's so good.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.348
I was so good at this.

00:01:46.348 --> 00:01:48.550
No streaming music or movies.

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:51.625
I really enjoyed using my Zune HD.

00:01:51.625 --> 00:01:55.410
Now we must get off the flight.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:56.783
We just landed in Detroit.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.190
Solid G3 service here.

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:02.068
It's 21 degrees fahrenheit right now.

00:02:02.068 --> 00:02:04.610
The driving part, not as easy.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:07.200
- [Man] All right, so
what's going on here?

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.240
- [Narrator] No GPS.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:13.930
It thinks we are in Wisconsin.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.150
We're not in Wisconsin.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.300
These are in Wisconsin still.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.270
Turns out that Garmin

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.060
didn't have the latest software update.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.260
Which needs to be downloaded
on a Windows computer

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.240
to reach the damn satellites.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.740
So I went back to 2000.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:29.803
But it looks like we've
gotta take 94 out of Detroit.

00:02:33.357 --> 00:02:34.350
Ah, Howell!

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:36.740
The maps got me close,
but not close enough.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:39.772
I had to call the hotel for directions.

00:02:39.772 --> 00:02:41.917
- [Woman On Phone] We're
just a couple exits down.

00:02:41.917 --> 00:02:43.590
- I'm so happy right now.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:47.350
The Holiday Inn Express in
Howell, which is close to Hell.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.750
Tomorrow we will go to Hell.

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:53.560
I asked the concierge to
print me out directions

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.853
from Howell to Hell.

00:02:57.011 --> 00:02:57.935
(trunk slams)

00:02:57.935 --> 00:02:59.197
(rock music)

00:02:59.197 --> 00:03:00.030
Do you know how to get to Hell?

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.636
- Just past the high
school on Darwin road.

00:03:02.636 --> 00:03:04.330
(rock music)

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:06.620
- I have been looking for
Darwin for quite a long time.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.153
- Okay, so that's gonna
be down here on your left.

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:10.880
- Get ice here before Hell freezes over.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.250
This is it.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:15.544
Look.

00:03:15.544 --> 00:03:17.463
Challenge complete.

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:20.590
Challenge two.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.840
Post a Selfie on Instagram.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.110
I really would like my
head to block the pure.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:27.053
Try this again.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:29.604
Nope.

00:03:29.604 --> 00:03:31.200
Okay.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.033
Nope.

00:03:34.499 --> 00:03:36.832
(beep)

00:03:36.832 --> 00:03:39.110
(growls)

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:42.110
My Selfie game was not good in 2010.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.793
Okay, now how to get these
photos on to Instagram.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.840
This shall be a challenge.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.871
Is there an internet cafe in Hell?

00:03:50.871 --> 00:03:53.220
- No, do you need to use the internet?

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.030
- [Narrator] I may need
to use the internet.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:56.590
- So you can just sign up to our WiFi.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.520
- [Narrator] The WiFi on my
BlackBerry wasn't gonna help,

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.870
since Instagram doesn't
have a BlackBerry app.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:02.890
So I hooked up the camera

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.363
to my new friend, Vaughn's Windows PC.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.418
I'm gonna import them all to her computer.

00:04:08.418 --> 00:04:10.190
I have no idea where these are going.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.603
Then, I got to Googling.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:15.453
Here, wait.

00:04:15.453 --> 00:04:16.286
This seems like a hack.

00:04:16.286 --> 00:04:17.860
I finally figured out a way.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.850
A Google Chrome trick for developers

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.770
that lets you force your web browser

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:23.698
to be like a phone's web browser.

00:04:23.698 --> 00:04:24.531
- That one's cute.

00:04:24.531 --> 00:04:25.370
- Which one, this one?

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:26.414
- [Vaughn] Yeah, that one's cute too.

00:04:26.414 --> 00:04:28.120
- [Narrator] Yeah, that one's good.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.682
Hello from Hell.

00:04:30.682 --> 00:04:32.390
I did it.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:34.380
Challenge complete.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.383
I feel pretty good.

00:04:35.383 --> 00:04:37.140
I'm also starving.

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:38.410
Challenge three.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.350
Review lunch on Yelp.

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:42.140
Its slim pickings on restaurants in Hell,

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:44.970
so I opted for the Hell Hole Bar,

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:46.880
and I ordered a local favorite.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:49.164
So I'm gonna be eating the Patsy.

00:04:49.164 --> 00:04:50.050
Patsty.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:50.990
Patsy?

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.336
What is it called?

00:04:52.336 --> 00:04:53.520
- [Man] Pasty.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.780
- [Narrator] This is called a pasty.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.950
This is a Michigan delicacy.

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:03.950
I'm eating a pasty and it
looks like a cross between

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.683
chicken pot pie and an empanada.

00:05:07.258 --> 00:05:09.010
It's really good.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:12.940
No posting my review was
well, not really possible.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:15.640
There was very little 3G
service in the restaurant.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.070
Like, the browser will load

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:20.150
but I can't really search
on the BlackBerry either.

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:22.740
The bigger issue was that
the BlackBerry 5 browser

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:25.520
was so slow to load images and the site,

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.490
and yes the iPhone 4 was out in 2010,

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.420
but I still had a BlackBerry.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:31.730
It was only hours later,

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.310
while sitting on the plane back home,

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.840
that I was able to log in and post it.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.475
Challenge complete.

00:05:37.475 --> 00:05:38.333
Kinda.

00:05:39.555 --> 00:05:43.483
Don't get me wrong, most of
my day in Hell was, hell.

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:47.450
Am I even in the photo?

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:49.903
But in many ways, it ended
up being like heaven.

00:05:50.894 --> 00:05:52.315
I don't even want to take a photo of this.

00:05:52.315 --> 00:05:53.615
It's that good.

00:05:53.615 --> 00:05:55.930
It was nice remembering
how we used to do things,

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.340
like navigate the world with our brains

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:00.650
or ask people to take photos of us.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:03.500
Best of all, it was nice to
remember when social media feeds

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:04.900
were just on computers

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:08.260
and unable to distract
us everywhere we are.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:12.170
I'm back from Hell, and here it is.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.183
I've made it.

00:06:14.119 --> 00:06:17.780
My iPhone.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:19.480
Would I do it again?

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:20.584
Hell no.

00:06:20.584 --> 00:06:23.300
(upbeat music)

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.113
Greetings from Hell, Mom.

